atlas commands-v6-owner

architecture v6-capability-bun-owner
  canonical_name V6CapabilityBunOwner
  family commands
  domain Execution / Resource evidence, mission candidates and representation distribution
  maturity implemented
  semantic_question Can one bounded owner compose resource observations, real substrate evidence, history verification and sparse representations without treating configuration or synthetic canaries as execution?
  purpose Replace V6 Python coordination with shared authenticated Bun transport and durable owners while preserving historical identities and refusing unsupported mission promotion.
  node_types ResourceObservation
  node_types BackendActivationEvidence
  node_types MissionCandidate
  node_types FederationRoot
  node_types SparseSnapshot
  internal_calculus one eighteen-operation catalog -> authenticated bounded transport -> confirmed STOP-gated owner -> durable attempt and completion or uncertainty
  internal_calculus raw numeric-source UTF-8 canonicalization -> row-bound receipt chain -> verified source-owner federation -> derived history root
  internal_calculus bounded source traversal -> pinned file or consistent SQLite snapshot -> sparse bundle -> content identity and explicit residency
  invariant all thirty-nine provider and fourteen backend contracts survive; configured credentials, binary help and source builds do not become semantic activation
  invariant probe bodies and credentials are not persisted; executable format checks reject Python trampolines
  invariant missing compiler or disabled compilation yields not-executed evidence and candidate missions, never synthetic passed canaries
  invariant STOP is checked at raw database and bundle publication boundaries as well as async owner boundaries
  invariant original receipt files and live source histories are never rewritten by federation verification
  forbidden_inference authenticated administrative routing or static analysis -> multi-tenant correctness, proven global scale or complete Python retirement
  forbidden_inference historical activation integrity -> fresh remote health or authority to execute effects
  source_path integrations/mcp/v6_catalog.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/v6_store.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/v6_schema.sql
  source_path integrations/mcp/v6_server.mjs
  source_path cmd/BonfyreMcp/src/clis.c
  source_path integrations/mcp/v6_resources.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/v6_history.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/v6_missions.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/project_owner.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/project_v6.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/v6_store.test.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/v6_transport.test.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/v6_resources.test.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/v6_history.test.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/v6_missions.test.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_v6.test.mjs
  witness tests/v6_history_witness.json thirty-one historical receipts verified on a disposable database/file copy; source bytes unchanged
  known_gap installed V6 service remains Python; source uses the real Bun compiler by default, but local canary ownership and full live cutover continuity remain incomplete
  known_gap source integrity manifests require trusted filesystem ownership; self-consistent hashes are not signed provenance or fresh execution attestation
  invariant ordinary BFP verification runs in a bounded two-worker executor by default; excess work refuses without queueing and cancellation never automatically replays a job
  source_path integrations/mcp/owned_worker_pool.mjs
  source_path integrations/mcp/v6_bfp_worker.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/owned_worker_pool.test.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/v6_bfp_worker_benchmark.mjs same archive and verifier compare main-event-loop interference with and without worker isolation
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/v6_bfp_worker_benchmark.json source-bound three-pair warmed 343295361-byte archive comparison; 64 section identities equal; maximum main-loop timer gap 549.01 ms direct versus 5.42 ms worker, similar verification time
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/v6_analysis.json Oxlint 1.86.0 analyzed 28 source-bound files with 96 rules and zero diagnostics
  invariant cooperative worker cancellation is observed between bounded verification reads through an atomic signal; noncooperative termination remains runtime-dependent
  known_gap receipt scans, SQLite checks and sparse packaging still occupy the owner event loop; isolating BFP alone does not prove acceptable whole-service tail latency
  forbidden_inference worker-thread isolation -> security sandbox, hardware resource quota or instantaneous hard preemption
  known_gap filesystem artifact publication and SQLite updates are not one transaction; interrupted operations require receipt-guided reconciliation

architecture v6-bfp-bounded-interchange
  canonical_name V6BfpBoundedInterchange
  family representation
  domain Representation / Streamed package and delta interchange
  maturity implemented
  semantic_question Can the same historical package and dictionary-delta contracts survive Python retirement without whole-package memory residency or unchecked extraction?
  internal_calculus manifest and section bounds -> streamed section digests -> pinned file identity -> optional confined extraction
  internal_calculus RAW or COPY_ADD or DEFLATE_DICT32 -> source digest and dictionary -> bounded reconstruction -> target digest
  invariant archive sources stream through bounded buffers; extraction requires verified section identity and confined destinations
  invariant native verifier output is corroborating evidence, not a substitute for structural validation
  forbidden_inference matching archive digests or small buffers -> optimal compression, hostile-filesystem race freedom or distributed deployment
  source_path integrations/mcp/v6_bfp.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/v6_bfp.test.mjs native corroboration, three codecs, deterministic packing, malformed bounds, tampering and symlink refusal
  known_gap selected delta codec is explicit rather than workload-measured automatic portfolio selection

interaction project-v6-reuses-semantic-owner
  source mcp-project-native-owner
  destination v6-capability-bun-owner
  relation catalog-bound-authenticated-owner-federation
  preserves exact schemas, dedicated HTTPS credentials, administrative closure, write admission and STOP
  drops endpoint selection by untrusted arguments and duplicated transport implementations
  forbidden_inference configured HTTPS and fixture forwarding -> deployed two-host execution
  binding integrations/mcp/project_owner.mjs
  binding integrations/mcp/project_v6.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/project_v6.test.mjs
  witness integrations/mcp/tests/oauth_institution_slice_test.sh

